  "query_preview": "..through this morning...Patchy fog is expected across\nthe higher terrain through early this morning, with some potential\nfor freezing fog in the usual colder locations. Therefore, some \nuntreated and elevated surfaces could be slick early this morning.\n\nThis afternoon...A cut-off low is currently spinning over northern\nArizona and southern Utah. As the low continues to lift northeastward,\ndrier air is ushered back into much of northern Arizona. A few \nisolated wrap-around showers and possibly a thunderstorm are \nexpected later this afternoon, mainly across the higher terrain of\nnortheastern Arizona. While a few brief heavy downpours could be \npossible, much of the rainfall looks to be light.\n\nMonday through Saturday...As the closed-low lifts into Colorado, \nweak ridging, or even quasi-zonal flow looks to build into the \nsouthwest. Gradually warming temperatures and dry conditions look to \nprevail through Thursday.\n\nA deepening trough over the Pacific Northwest looks to breakdown \nthis pattern near the end of next week. Cooler temperatures and a \nreturn of precipitation look probable near the end of the week as a \nresult.",
